{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551946424,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3MDQyODE4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3204#issuecomment-470428186"},"message":"Tangentially related issue: I think we should align ourselves more with git-annex re this kind of options (we can still have dedicated commandline opts to trigger them). In particular, I think we should support this kind of call:\n\n`datalad -c annex.largefiles=... add/rev-save`\n\nATM `rev-save` still has `--to-git` that does too complicated things, but it should really do `annex.largfiles=nothing`.\n\nAt the core, this would mean to make `AnnexRepo.add` call git-annex with a properly adjusted configuration. That piece of code is used both by -core and -revolution.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1551969368,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3MDU0OTMzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3204#issuecomment-470549334"},"message":"\u003e I think we should align ourselves more with git-annex re this kind of options (we can still have dedicated commandline opts to trigger them). In particular, I think we should support this kind of call:\n\u003e\n\u003e `datalad -c annex.largefiles=... add/rev-save`\n\nFrom a UI perspective I like the consistency.  My one reservation is that the consistency could cause confusion: Would users see that and think \"oh, I can pass along `-c annex.*` options to any underlying git annex command\"?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551969836,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3MDU1MTg1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3204#issuecomment-470551856"},"message":"I see it as \"specifying ad-hoc configuration that also (and that is the new part) affect underlying calls (plural) to git and git-annex\", but not additional options for a particular call. The latter we tried to achieve with the old `annex-opts` -- and failed, due to the lack of precise association of options with specific calls. Resorting/restricting to configuration items should not have this issue.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551969836,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE5MzM2NzAwMQ=="},"target":"5e82b42a3f3af34910d605fb1a63277b18abd87b792057ca7fa66625a09b5b78","message":"I see it as \"specifying ad-hoc configuration that also (and that is the new part) affect underlying calls (plural) to git and git-annex\", but not additional options for a particular call. The latter we tried to achieve with the old `annex-opts` -- and failed, due to the lack of precise association of options with specific calls. Resorting/restricting to configuration items should not have this issue.\n\nThat being said, we *could* have `to-git`, which could be implemented as `annex.largefiles=nothing` within `rev-save`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578605695,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3Mjc2NzAyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3204#issuecomment-572767029"},"message":"This isn't worth keeping open now that `add` is obsolete and the 0.12.0 release is near.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578605696,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjkzNjU0MTc5NA=="},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578605704,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5MzY1NDIxNjA="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]}]}